# Anthropic API key
# If you want to use your Claude subscription instead of an API key, see https://github.com/mattpocock/sandcastle/issues/191
CLAUDE_CODE_OAUTH_TOKEN=
# GitHub personal access token — use a FINE-GRAINED PAT scoped to THIS repo only
# (contents / issues / pull-requests: read-write; workflows RW only if the
# pipeline edits .github/). Never a classic repo-scope token: the sandbox is the
# least-trusted context in the system and must not hold a credential that
# reaches any other repository.
GH_TOKEN=

# ─── Turbo remote cache ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# TURBO_TOKEN and TURBO_TEAM are read from your host shell environment, NOT
# from this file. This is intentional: putting credentials in .env adds a
# stale-token footgun and leaks them to git if .env is ever committed by mistake.
#
# To enable the Vercel remote cache (same cache CI uses), run once in your
# terminal:
#
#   turbo login && turbo link
#
# After that, `turbo` writes TURBO_TOKEN and TURBO_TEAM to ~/.turbo/config.json
# and exports them automatically. Re-run `pnpm sandcastle` and you will see:
#   [turbo] remote cache enabled (TURBO_TOKEN=... chars, TURBO_TEAM=... chars)
#
# If either variable is missing, sandcastle prints a warning and continues
# without remote cache — sandbox runs still work, just slower (cold inputs).
